==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|colourise}} {{qualifier|UK}}

* [[colourize]] {{qualifier|Canada}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|color|ize}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|coloriz}}

# To add color to.
#: ''The child '''colorized''' the drawing.''
#: ''The woman '''colorized''' her hair.''
# {{lb|en|photography|filmology}} To convert [[black and white]] media to [[color]] by digital post production {{qualifier|as is often done in digital photography and in video special effects}}.
#: ''There is a '''colorized''' version of Casablanca.''
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=August 26, 1988|author=[[w:Jonathan Rosenbaum|Jonathan Rosenbaum]]|title=Looking for America|work=Chicago Reader|url=https://securesite.chireader.com/cgi-bin/Archive/abridged2.bat?path=1988/880826/SENSES
|passage=What we see are beautiful overlapping NASA satellite photographs of the American mainland, {{...|proceeding sequentially from the east to the west--photographs}}taken in black and white and then luminously '''colorized''' by computer for scientific reasons.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to add color to}} {{l|en|color}} ([[colour]]), [[color in]] ([[colour in]])

====Antonyms====
